# Xray

Xray is the VLESS engine. Python orchestrates via `asyncio.create_subprocess_exec()`.

## Configuration

- Binary path from `XRAY_PATH` env var (default `xray`). Never hardcode paths.
- Each concurrent test gets its own temp config, Xray process, SOCKS5 port, timeout, and cleanup.
- Always terminate Xray and delete temp config files after each test.

## Health criteria

A config is healthy only when HTTP/HTTPS succeeds through the SOCKS5 proxy. TCP connect alone is insufficient.

## VLESS parsing

- Parse URLs with `urllib.parse` in `utils/proxy/`.
- Support tcp, ws, grpc, xhttp transports; tls and reality security.
- Fragment/name is display-only — never use it as proof of geographic location.
